\b 3) Fast review path\b0\par
\par
Please use the following path for the quickest review:\par
1. Launch the app.\par
2. On the public experience, browse available properties/listings.\par
3. Sign in with the guest test account above, or create a new account from the Register screen.\par
4. Open the profile area to confirm account/profile management.\par
5. Navigate to booking/reservation views to review reservation and messaging workflows.\par
6. To review host features, sign in with the host account above.\par
7. Open Pricing to review the subscription/plan selection screen.\par
8. Open Profile to review subscription management and billing portal entry points.\par
9. Open Add Property to review host listing creation, location selection, and photo upload flows.\par
10. Open Support to review help resources and support/contact flows.\par
\par
\b 4) Features that may require explanation during review\b0\par
\par
\b Authentication\b0\par
- Users can register and sign in from the app.\par
- If a test account is provided above, no invitation code or special approval is required.\par
\par
\b Property browsing and booking\b0\par
- The app includes property browsing, property details, reservation-related views, and message/unread activity indicators.\par
\par
\b Host Account\b0\par
- Host plans are presented on the screen.\par
- Account management is available from Profile.\par
- Billing does not need to be completed to review the app's core browse, account, reservation, messaging, and support flows.\par
- If needed, the reviewer can inspect the Pricing screen and subscription-management entry points without completing a purchase.\par
- In the iOS app build, external subscription checkout and billing portal launches are disabled; no in-app external payment flow is initiated during review.\par
\par
\b Support / communication\b0\par
- The app includes support resources and reservation-related communication flows.\par
- Unread message indicators are updated in-app.\par
- Email notification preferences can be managed from Profile/Support.\par
\par
\b 5) Permissions and device behavior\b0\par
\par
\b Photos\b0\par
- The app can open the system photo/file picker for optional profile photos and property images.\par
- Camera access is not required.\par
- If users choose image capture/upload, iOS permission prompts include explicit, purpose-limited messaging.\par
\par
\b Location / maps\b0\par
- The app uses map-based location selection and map display for listings.\par
- Location can be selected manually on the map and via address search.\par
- If the build does not request device GPS permission, the reviewer can still complete this flow manually.\par
\par
\b Notifications\b0\par
- This build does not rely on Apple Push Notification permission for core review flows.\par
- Notification-style updates in the app are primarily in-app unread/status indicators and optional email preferences.\par
\par
